{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1254087-lore-of-the-realms-question-dtf-core-book-p-213","id":1254087,"title":"Lore of the Realms Question (DtF core book, p.213)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-13T21:01:50-07:00","id":1254087,"title":"Lore of the Realms Question (DtF core book, p.213)","content":"Once the demon has crossed the barrier and stepped into the shadow world, can the demon perceive the individuals inhabiting the mortal world? If yes, would Step Beyond the Veil (Level Two) be enough for that or would the demon need Reach Across the Barrier (Level Four)?<br /> <br /> There is no doubt that can be done using Ghost Walk (Level Three) but the issue is that Ghost Walk creates an image of the demon in the mortal world. The demon basically wants to spectate the individuals in the mortal world from the shadow world without being seen by the mortal world inhabitants.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>** Step Beyond the Veil</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This evocation allows the Slayer to physically cross the barrier into the shadow world, a lifeless mirror image of the mortal world. </div> </div> </div>The book mentions &quot;lifeless mirror image&quot; - would that mean the mortals cannot be perceived using this power as they are everything but lifeless?<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>**** Reach Across the Barrier</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Slayer can peer into and reach across into the spirit realm the same way a mortal retrieves something from a cupboard, placing or retrieving items between the realms at will. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your roll is successful, your character can see into and \u201creach\u201d across the barrier between realms - her hand and arm literally vanishes from mortal eyes until she withdraws it again. </div> </div> </div>Here it specifically says that the demon can see across the barrier between the realms. Correct me if I'm wrong but in order to spectate someone from the shadow world into the mortal world, would the demon need to enter the shadow world using Step Beyond the Veil and then use Reach Across the Barrier to peek into the mortal world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10423-rudy23","user":"Rudy23","date":". 09-14-2018, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10423-rudy23","name":"Rudy23","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T22:05:28-07:00","id":1254097,"title":"","content":"Hello. I've also posed <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG/comments/86ch1q/dtfseeing_through_the_veil_lore_of_the_realms/\" target=\"_blank\">this question on WhiteWolf's</a> reddit and someone had said it is the nature of the veil that allows its inhabitants to see through. Though they did not provide any reference, I did run into several cases depicting wraiths being able to perceive mortals and their ongoings in the skinlands, thus reaching the conclusion that rather than being an inherent ability of spirits, it's just the way the shadowlands are.<br /> <br /> Although generally speaking dtf's details into the matter are kinda lacking, I did find this to be a compelling argument.<br /> <i>Demon: The Fallen (The Storyteller's Companion page 51-52)</i> The shadowlands paragraph &amp; the one above it<br /> <br /> The newest Wraith: The Oblivion has a more detailed approach when it comes to the veils, but on the other hand it lacks a clear definition if fallen are included into it.<br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/Hl5ef9S.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> What this shows is their ability to spectate the ongoings of living beings. In addition to that (refer to however), they also have deathsight which allows them to prey on death marked humans. The latter does not apply to fallen (given the existence of the ability Deathsight (tho I may have the name wrong), which would make it redundant.)<br /> <br /> An additional hint can be found in the idea that says Slayers are particularly used by the Eagles/Dragons ministries due to their proficiency with the underworld.<br /> Anyhow, we've posted this question in a Q&amp;A thread before but got no reply, so I'm quite eager to see your replies.<br /> Thank you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13665-ravencorella","name":"RavenCorella","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T03:30:30-07:00","id":1254128,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rudy23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1254087-lore-of-the-realms-question-dtf-core-book-p-213#post1254087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once the demon has crossed the barrier and stepped into the shadow world, can the demon perceive the individuals inhabiting the mortal world? If yes, would Step Beyond the Veil (Level Two) be enough for that or would the demon need Reach Across the Barrier (Level Four)?<br /> <br /> There is no doubt that can be done using Ghost Walk (Level Three) but the issue is that Ghost Walk creates an image of the demon in the mortal world. The demon basically wants to spectate the individuals in the mortal world from the shadow world without being seen by the mortal world inhabitants. <hr /><br /> <b>** Step Beyond the Veil</b><br /> <br /> The book mentions &quot;lifeless mirror image&quot; - would that mean the mortals cannot be perceived using this power as they are everything but lifeless? <hr /><br /> <b>**** Reach Across the Barrier</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Here it specifically says that the demon can see across the barrier between the realms. Correct me if I'm wrong but in order to spectate someone from the shadow world into the mortal world, would the demon need to enter the shadow world using Step Beyond the Veil and then use Reach Across the Barrier to peek into the mortal world?</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, hello from the beyond, I\u2019ll give my two oboli regarding the matter since I've had this issue in one of my chronicles,<br /> first it's the shadowlands not shadow world, those are two completely different worlds.<br /> Shadowlands is the first layer of the haven aka the underworld created by the slayers if we\u2019re following dtf and the home of the wraiths while the shadow world is the lifeless mirror world accessed via Portals 5 Doorway into Darkness.<br /> <br /> Now regarding your question, it\u2019s a yes and a no, if we\u2019re talking the first layer of the haven aka the shadowlands then yes, he can perceive the living world and its inhabitants yet by \u201clifeless\u201d it means the world would have a sort grey hue to it, decayed, corrupted and overall rotten and sad, that what it meant by lifeless.<br /> <br /> The scenery in the Underworld can rarely be described as \u201cbeautiful., so by lifeless mirror, it would reflect the skinlands ( living world ) as a pale reflection of itself, that ability itself gave the Halaku their feared reputation, quoting Crowley here \u201cno door, no wall, could keep the reaper at bay\u201d, giving them an edge on tracking and finding their targets plus giving them the ability to wonder further into the shadowlands via byways or nihils but that\u2019s plain stupid for any non-suicidal demon who doesn\u2019t at least have Lore of the spirit.<br /> <br /> As I recall from dtf fiction (pardon me it\u2019s been a while), Usiel used many times to get his opponents offguard, it gave all slayers that fearful reputation of harbingers of death.<br /> <br /> Now to clear realms 4, I honestly st as a way to store items in a pocket dimension \u201cbetween realms\u201d instead a way of interacting due the ability of it to become ridiculously broken, placing a sharp sword rapidly in the skin lands that manifest right in someone\u2019s heart, that\u2019s troubling but that\u2019s up to your st to decide really.<br /> <br /> Now my opinion, it\u2019s unrealistic to say the demon would be unable to perceive the world of living like the wraith can, it makes the lore tenfold risky to use as it currently is and reduce a lot of its functionality as a lore since the demon won't know where will he lands, manifesting himself infront of a crowd of people would be troubling or at the front of a firing squad .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RavenCorella</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1254087-lore-of-the-realms-question-dtf-core-book-p-213?p=1254097#post1254097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello. I've also posed <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG/comments/86ch1q/dtfseeing_through_the_veil_lore_of_the_realms/\" target=\"_blank\">this question on WhiteWolf's</a> reddit and someone had said it is the nature of the veil that allows its inhabitants to see through. Though they did not provide any reference, I did run into several cases depicting wraiths being able to perceive mortals and their ongoings in the skinlands, thus reaching the conclusion that rather than being an inherent ability of spirits, it's just the way the shadowlands are.<br /> <br /> Although generally speaking dtf's details into the matter are kinda lacking, I did find this to be a compelling argument.<br /> <i>Demon: The Fallen (The Storyteller's Companion page 51-52)</i> The shadowlands paragraph &amp; the one above it<br /> <br /> The newest Wraith: The Oblivion has a more detailed approach when it comes to the veils, but on the other hand it lacks a clear definition if fallen are included into it.<br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/Hl5ef9S.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> What this shows is their ability to spectate the ongoings of living beings. In addition to that (refer to however), they also have deathsight which allows them to prey on death marked humans. The latter does not apply to fallen (given the existence of the ability Deathsight (tho I may have the name wrong), which would make it redundant.)<br /> <br /> An additional hint can be found in the idea that says Slayers are particularly used by the Eagles/Dragons ministries due to their proficiency with the underworld.<br /> Anyhow, we've posted this question in a Q&amp;A thread before but got no reply, so I'm quite eager to see your replies.<br /> Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey there, first it\u2019s really understandable that WTO doesn\u2019t mention DTF since some metaphysical toes would stepped upon.<br /> Second deathsight and lifesight are quite explained, one works pretty much like auspex in vtm<br /> <br /> <b> wraiths can also see life. Every wraith is capable of seeing the auras around living beings, the swirling shells of color that change from moment to moment according to their health, mood, and state of mind. With a little practice, wraiths can use this ability to get a reading on what one of the Quick is likely to do next, and if they\u2019re lying</b><br /> <br /> While death sight is a sort of a dark perception twist, it allows them to see the decay of the world and the taint of oblivion.<br /> <br /> Again my two oboli, enjoy!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.com/v2/137x125q90/661/nSdTJk.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8612-magnus666","name":"magnus666","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T05:33:54-07:00","id":1254148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magnus666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1254087-lore-of-the-realms-question-dtf-core-book-p-213?p=1254128#post1254128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now my opinion, it\u2019s unrealistic to say the demon would be unable to perceive the world of living like the wraith can, it makes the lore tenfold risky to use as it currently is and reduce a lot of its functionality as a lore since the demon won't know where will he lands, manifesting himself infront of a crowd of people would be troubling or at the front of a firing squad .</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand your perspective, but it would be really unrealistic to claim that the demon is able to perceive the world of living like a wraith can. It specifically says in the Demon's Storyteller Companion that the Veil has been warped by the effects of centuries of human disbelief and now it became an unyielding wall that resists even the fallen who helped raise it. How would you go about seeing through the Veil, that's separating the two worlds, instinctively like that?<br /> <br /> It doesn't make it risky, a good Slayer who is well acknowledged of the area surrounding him would certainly know how to maneuver through the Shadowlands and appear in places correspondent to the material world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rudy23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1254087-lore-of-the-realms-question-dtf-core-book-p-213#post1254087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>** Step Beyond the Veil</b><br /> The book mentions &quot;lifeless mirror image&quot; - would that mean the mortals cannot be perceived using this power as they are everything but lifeless? <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magnus666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1254087-lore-of-the-realms-question-dtf-core-book-p-213?p=1254128#post1254128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now regarding your question, it\u2019s a yes and a no, if we\u2019re talking the first layer of the haven aka the shadowlands then yes, he can perceive the living world and its inhabitants yet by \u201clifeless\u201d it means the world would have a sort grey hue to it, decayed, corrupted and overall rotten and sad, that what it meant by lifeless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe that's the perception of the living world, that's how the Shadowlands looks like -- just as the Penumbra has the &quot;mirror&quot; aspect of the material world, the Shadowlands has the decayed, death and sorrowful (lifeless) aspect of the material world. That's how it's manifested, not how the material world is perceived from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","user":"Darko","date":". 09-14-2018, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","name":"Darko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11698_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T06:10:22-07:00","id":1254154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magnus666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1254087-lore-of-the-realms-question-dtf-core-book-p-213?p=1254128#post1254128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, hello from the beyond, I\u2019ll give my two oboli regarding the matter since I've had this issue in one of my chronicles,<br /> first it's the shadowlands not shadow world, those are two completely different worlds.<br /> Shadowlands is the first layer of the haven aka the underworld created by the slayers if we\u2019re following dtf and the home of the wraiths while the shadow world is the lifeless mirror world accessed via Portals 5 Doorway into Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure in DtF the writer referes to the same thing when using the terms shadow world, shadow lands and shadow realm. Read the full description of Step Beyond the Veil and you'll see what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magnus666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1254087-lore-of-the-realms-question-dtf-core-book-p-213?p=1254128#post1254128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the shadow world is the lifeless mirror world accessed via Portals 5 Doorway into Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can access it via Step Beyond the Veil as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10423-rudy23","name":"Rudy23","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T07:15:18-07:00","id":1254184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1254087-lore-of-the-realms-question-dtf-core-book-p-213?p=1254148#post1254148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand your perspective, but it would be really unrealistic to claim that the demon is able to perceive the world of living like a wraith can. It specifically says in the Demon's Storyteller Companion that the Veil has been warped by the effects of centuries of human disbelief and now it became an unyielding wall that resists even the fallen who helped raise it. How would you go about seeing through the Veil, that's separating the two worlds, instinctively like that?<br /> <br /> It doesn't make it risky, a good Slayer who is well acknowledged of the area surrounding him would certainly know how to maneuver through the Shadowlands and appear in places correspondent to the material world.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't believe that's the perception of the living world, that's how the Shadowlands looks like -- just as the Penumbra has the &quot;mirror&quot; aspect of the material world, the Shadowlands has the decayed, death and sorrowful (lifeless) aspect of the material world. That's how it's manifested, not how the material world is perceived from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaia fan alert, Charon forbid! jk<br /> Seriously though, it\u2019s true the shroud has been corrupted, hardened by eons of maltreatment, making harder for the fallen to pass through yet visibility is the same it\u2019s like a silky smooth transparent pure silk turned into a hard transparent mirror, you could still see but it becomes hard to interact with, in the words of the OG devil himself<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=599iGGPJ3OQ\" data-code=\"599iGGPJ3OQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/599iGGPJ3OQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> And no a fallen can\u2019t perceive the living world as a wraith can lol, a demon looking through the shroud would see well the same living world albeit decayed and grim, people would remain \u2026well\u2026..people yet when a wraith see it, they see that and much more if they have the right powers, they see the aura\u2019s of the living , the taint of oblivion and more but there\u2019s nothing stopping a demon from seeing the inhabitants of the skinlands.<br /> <br /> Now I have no idea about the umbra and the penumbra from wta games but is it impossible to perceive the living world from them? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rudy23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1254087-lore-of-the-realms-question-dtf-core-book-p-213?p=1254154#post1254154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure in DtF the writer referes to the same thing when using the terms shadow world, shadow lands and shadow realm. Read the full description of Step Beyond the Veil and you'll see what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> <u>You can access it via Step Beyond the Veil as well.</u></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You might be right, but here the thing going into the shadowlands doesn\u2019t make you suffer 1 bashing per day unlike Realms 5 which if we follow you, does the same thing but again it does state \u201cshadowlands \u201c in the torment description, idk really I\u2019ll check the book later for more details but it\u2019s best to leave it to your gm to define it.<br /> <br /> By shadow realm you mean another name for the shadowlands or the entire haven aka the underworld ?<br /> <br /> since going to the tempest without a byway or the labyrinth would be suicide for most demons or any unlucky bastard who ends there but the shadowlands is fine and more manageable although sill risky.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.com/v2/137x125q90/661/nSdTJk.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8612-magnus666","name":"magnus666","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T07:15:46-07:00","id":1254186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It specifically says in the Demon's Storyteller Companion that the Veil has been warped by the effects of centuries of human disbelief and now it became an unyielding wall that resists even the fallen who helped raise it. </div> </div> </div>@Darko: That obviously refers to stepping <b>from the skinlands into the shadowlands</b>. I don't know how many times I have to point out that it is the other way around. A demon peers from the other side. Crossing over <b>from</b> the shadowlands <b>into</b> the skinlands also happens to be reflexive. How do you explain the lack of difficulty to leave if the veil isn't weaker from the inside? It was designed to let the souls of the dead return with time, which is what wraiths are capable of doing in seams and ripples in the veil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I understand your perspective, but it would be really unrealistic to claim that the demon is able to perceive the world of living like a wraith can. </div> </div> </div><i>Are you seriously bringing up realism in a World of Darkness game?</i> What exactly is unrealistic about it? Why is it unrealistic? Where in the book does it say it is unrealistic? Seeing past the veil from within is not an ability of wraiths, so demons don't share the same characteristics - no. On the other hand, the veil has been made that way.<br /> <br /> In either case, let's not argue about this here and rather wait for third party inputs.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13665-ravencorella","user":"RavenCorella","date":". 09-14-2018, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13665-ravencorella","name":"RavenCorella","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T07:47:35-07:00","id":1254203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RavenCorella</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1254087-lore-of-the-realms-question-dtf-core-book-p-213?p=1254186#post1254186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Are you seriously bringing up realism in a World of Darkness game?</i> What exactly is unrealistic about it? Why is it unrealistic? Where in the book does it say it is unrealistic? Seeing past the veil from within is not an ability of wraiths, so demons don't share the same characteristics - no. On the other hand, the veil has been made that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it was <b>magnus666</b> who brought that statement when it comes to realism, I have only responded in accord to his statement and nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","name":"Darko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.co